    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "My lua config sets line numbers on.\r\n\r\nHowever, I want to use mini.starter with the example in the readme:\r\n```\r\nnow(function()\r\n  local starter = require('mini.starter')\r\n\tstarter.setup({\r\n\t\tautoopen = true,\r\n    evaluate_single = true,\r\n    items = {\r\n      starter.sections.builtin_actions(),\r\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, false),\r\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, true),\r\n      starter.sections.sessions(5, true)\r\n    },\r\n    content_hooks = {\r\n      starter.gen_hook.adding_bullet(),\r\n      starter.gen_hook.indexing('all', { 'Builtin actions' }),\r\n      starter.gen_hook.padding(3, 2),\r\n    },\r\n}) end)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat I'm finding tho is the starter page starts with `set nonumbers`. \r\nIs there a way to turn `set numbers` back on after the starter page is dismissed?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">My lua config sets line numbers on.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, I want to use mini.starter with the example in the readme:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"now(function()\n  local starter = require('mini.starter')\n\tstarter.setup({\n\t\tautoopen = true,\n    evaluate_single = true,\n    items = {\n      starter.sections.builtin_actions(),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, false),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, true),\n      starter.sections.sessions(5, true)\n    },\n    content_hooks = {\n      starter.gen_hook.adding_bullet(),\n      starter.gen_hook.indexing('all', { 'Builtin actions' }),\n      starter.gen_hook.padding(3, 2),\n    },\n}) end)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">now(function()\n  local starter = require('mini.starter')\n\tstarter.setup({\n\t\tautoopen = true,\n    evaluate_single = true,\n    items = {\n      starter.sections.builtin_actions(),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, false),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, true),\n      starter.sections.sessions(5, true)\n    },\n    content_hooks = {\n      starter.gen_hook.adding_bullet(),\n      starter.gen_hook.indexing('all', { 'Builtin actions' }),\n      starter.gen_hook.padding(3, 2),\n    },\n}) end)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What I'm finding tho is the starter page starts with <code class=\"notranslate\">set nonumbers</code>.<br>\nIs there a way to turn <code class=\"notranslate\">set numbers</code> back on after the starter page is dismissed?</p>",
    "bodyText": "My lua config sets line numbers on.\nHowever, I want to use mini.starter with the example in the readme:\nnow(function()\n  local starter = require('mini.starter')\n\tstarter.setup({\n\t\tautoopen = true,\n    evaluate_single = true,\n    items = {\n      starter.sections.builtin_actions(),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, false),\n      starter.sections.recent_files(10, true),\n      starter.sections.sessions(5, true)\n    },\n    content_hooks = {\n      starter.gen_hook.adding_bullet(),\n      starter.gen_hook.indexing('all', { 'Builtin actions' }),\n      starter.gen_hook.padding(3, 2),\n    },\n}) end)\n\nWhat I'm finding tho is the starter page starts with set nonumbers.\nIs there a way to turn set numbers back on after the starter page is dismissed?",
